From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Wed, 22 Apr 2026 10:06:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] pcie: mediatek-gen3: disable async probe

The 6.18 driver sets PROBE_PREFER_ASYNCHRONOUS (absent in 6.12).
With the Mediatek wifi-reset flow, the driver sleeps a long time 
inside probe (100ms reset pulse + 500ms deassert settle).
Running that asynchronously lets other drivers init in parallel,
and on MT7988A + MT7996 the resulting ordering leaves the RC's
LTSSM wedged at detect.quiet. Link training never starts even
though MAC/PERST# sequencing is correct.

Dropping the async hint restores the synchronous probe ordering
used by 6.12 and recovers link training on boards that pulse the
WiFi chip reset GPIO during probe.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/pcie-mediatek-gen3.c |    1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-mediatek-gen3.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-mediatek-gen3.c
@@ -1413,7 +1413,6 @@ static struct platform_driver mtk_pcie_d
 		.name = "mtk-pcie-gen3",
 		.of_match_table = mtk_pcie_of_match,
 		.pm = &mtk_pcie_pm_ops,
-		.probe_type = PROBE_PREFER_ASYNCHRONOUS,
 	},
 };
 
